{"availability":"available","full":"dragonked2/alphacode","name":"alphacode","description":"Free MIT AI coding agent — no API key needed. Built-in free model, or bring Claude, GPT, Gemini, DeepSeek, Ollama +50 more. Swarm mode, 40+ tools, browser & desktop automation, built in Rust.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Rust","stars":265,"forks":18,"created":"2026-09-01T09:57:03Z","updated":"2026-10-11T01:56:06Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://alphacli.github.io/","topics":["agentic-ai","ai","ai-agent","ai-agents","ai-coding","ai-coding-assistant","ai-tools","autonomous-agents","cli","code-assistant","coding-agent","developer-tools","free-ai","llm","llm-agent","no-api-key","ollama","openai-compatible","rust","terminal"],"demo":"https://alphacli.github.io/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T04:29:40.256Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T04:29:40.256Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T04:29:40.256Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T04:29:40.256Z","stars":265,"forks":18}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A terminal-first AI coding agent that can understand a codebase, edit files, run commands and tests, automate Firefox, control desktop applications, and verify its work.","Get started · Documentation · Releases · Report a bug · Firefox Browser Agent","AlphaCode is an open-source AI coding agent built in Rust. Instead of only suggesting code in a chat, it can work in your development environment: inspect a repository, plan a task, edit files, run commands and tests, use web tools, operate a real Firefox session, interact with desktop applications, and report what it verified."],"features":["Use AlphaCode to explore an unfamiliar codebase, trace a bug, refactor a module, add a feature, run a build, create regression tests, review a diff, or investigate a failure.","Combine web tools with a real browser to inspect dynamic pages, interact with forms, validate user flows, capture screens